# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Zenith OS — Environment Variables Template
# Phase 2 · Step 2.2 — Cloud Synchronization Pipeline
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your Supabase project values.
# .env.local is gitignored and never committed.
#
# Where to find these values:
#   Supabase Dashboard → Your Project → Settings → API
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Your Supabase project URL (e.g. https://xxxxxxxxxxxx.supabase.co)
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=

# Your Supabase project public anon key (safe to expose in the browser)
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# AI features — OPTIONAL server-side fallback key
#
# Users can supply their OWN key in-app (Settings → AI Provider) — that
# key is stored only in their browser and billed to their own account.
# The variable below is only a fallback used when no user key is present
# (e.g. your own local dev). SERVER-SIDE ONLY — never prefix NEXT_PUBLIC_.
#
# Accepts either provider; the app auto-detects from the key prefix:
#   • Anthropic Claude  →  sk-ant-...   (https://console.anthropic.com)
#   • Google Gemini     →  AIza...      (https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey)
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Fallback API key (sk-ant-... for Claude, or AIza... for Gemini)
LLM_API_KEY=

# Optional: override the Anthropic model (used when key is an sk-ant- key)
# Available: claude-haiku-4-5-20251001 | claude-sonnet-4-6 | claude-opus-4-8
LLM_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5-20251001

# Optional: override the Gemini model (used when key is an AIza key)
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.0-flash

# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Microsoft Calendar direct sync — OPTIONAL (~5-minute setup)
#
# When set, the Universal Calendar can push personal events straight into a
# user's Microsoft 365 / Outlook calendar via Microsoft Graph (MSAL popup
# sign-in). When UNSET, the app degrades gracefully: the instant
# "Add to Outlook Calendar" deep-link still works for everyone with no login.
#
# This is a PUBLIC client ID (a single-page-app / SPA client). It is safe to
# expose in the browser bundle — hence the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix. There is no
# client secret involved (SPAs use PKCE, not secrets).
#
# Setup:
#   1. Azure Portal → App registrations → New registration.
#   2. Supported account types: "Accounts in any organizational directory
#      and personal Microsoft accounts" (multi-tenant + personal).
#   3. Platform configuration → add a "Single-page application (SPA)" platform.
#      Redirect URIs = your site origin(s), e.g.:
#         https://your-app.vercel.app
#         http://localhost:3000
#   4. API permissions → Add → Microsoft Graph → Delegated →
#      Calendars.ReadWrite  (User.Read is included by default).
#   5. Copy the "Application (client) ID" from the Overview page → paste below.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Azure App registration Application (client) ID — PUBLIC, safe to expose.
NEXT_PUBLIC_MS_CLIENT_ID=

# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Feedback & legal contact — OPTIONAL
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Web3Forms access key for the in-app "Report an Issue" form
# (https://web3forms.com — the key routes submissions to your inbox without
# exposing the email address; public-by-design but kept out of source).
# Leave empty to disable the feedback form gracefully.
NEXT_PUBLIC_WEB3FORMS_KEY=

# Contact shown in the Privacy Policy / Terms of Service. Use a role-based
# address (e.g. support@yourdomain.com) or a contact-form URL — NOT a
# personal email. Leave empty to point users at the in-app feedback form.
NEXT_PUBLIC_LEGAL_CONTACT=

# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Cloud Snapshot — whole-database sync between browser profiles
#
# Every browser profile has its own isolated IndexedDB, so two Edge profiles
# (school / personal) on the same laptop hold two divergent copies of Zenith.
# Cloud Snapshot fixes that by storing your ENTIRE local database as one row
# per account in Supabase, with last-write-wins conflict resolution.
#
# It reuses the NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_* variables above — there is nothing new
# to add here. Two one-time setup steps are required:
#
#   1. Run the migration. Open Supabase Dashboard -> SQL Editor, paste the
#      contents of:
#         supabase/migrations/20260803000001_cloud_snapshot.sql
#      and Run. This creates the `zenith_snapshots` table plus its RLS
#      policies (all scoped to user_id = auth.uid()) and updated_at trigger.
#
#   2. Sign in with a real account (email + password). Cloud Snapshot needs a
#      genuine Supabase user id; the "Continue offline" local-only session has
#      no auth.uid() and stays entirely on the device.
#
# Once both are done, Settings -> Cloud Sync shows the panel: the workspace
# auto-saves a few seconds after you stop making changes (and when the tab is
# hidden or closed), and auto-loads on sign-in whenever the cloud copy is
# newer than this profile and this profile has nothing unsaved.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Strava — OPTIONAL watch import (~5-minute setup)
#
# Zenith reads workouts from Strava rather than from a watch directly.
# Garmin's own Connect API is behind a company-approval developer
# programme and speaks OAuth 1.0a; there is no consumer key to get. Most
# watches — Garmin, Wahoo, Coros, Polar, Apple via a bridge — already
# push to Strava automatically, so Strava is the road in.
#
# When UNSET, the Workouts → Cardio tab simply says the feature is not
# configured and the manual log works exactly as before.
#
# These are SERVER-SIDE ONLY. The client secret must never carry a
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix, and the tokens live in an httpOnly cookie rather
# than localStorage: a Strava refresh token is a long-lived credential
# for an account that knows where you run.
#
# Setup:
#   1. https://www.strava.com/settings/api → Create & Manage Your App.
#   2. Authorization Callback Domain: your host WITHOUT scheme or path —
#        your-app.vercel.app        (production)
#        localhost                  (local development)
#      Strava allows exactly one domain per app, so a separate app for
#      local development is usually easier than swapping it back and forth.
#   3. Copy the Client ID and Client Secret below.
#
# Zenith requests `activity:read_all` and nothing else — read-only, and it
# never posts to Strava. On the consent screen the activity checkbox has
# to be ticked; approving without it connects the account but returns no
# activities, and the app will tell you so rather than looking broken.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

STRAVA_CLIENT_ID=
STRAVA_CLIENT_SECRET=
